; West Virginia's estimated tax: W. Va. Code §§ 11-21-55, 11-21-56,
; 11-10-17a and 11-10-18a, worked through on Form IT-210, which follows
; federal Form 2210's shape. It is written on the shared machinery in
; returns/rules/federal/10_estimated_lib.tlisp and reproduces the Go rules in
; westvirginiataxcalc/estimated.go, whose answers
; golden/testdata/estimated/WV.json.gz holds.
;
; The figures follow the Tax Division's penalty form, Form IT-210 in the 2025
; IT-140 booklet, the latest published, and the IT-140ESI (Sept 2023) for who
; must pay; the answer's divergences say where the Code reads otherwise. The
; target is the smaller of 90% of this year's tax and 100% of last year's,
; with no 110% tier; a zero tax last year counts only while this year's tax
; is $5,000 or less. The penalty is charged at the daily factor the form
; prints, each charge in whole dollars. A year with no figures is answered
; ESTIMATED_OUTCOME_NO_RULES.

; One tax year's figures, as the Tax Division's TSD-365 prints them for the
; year.
(defstruct WestVirginiaEstimatedYear
  (tax_year Int)
  ; § 11-10-17a(c): the rate for the calendar year, in basis points.
  (annual_rate Int))

(deffigures wv-estimated-2026 WestVirginiaEstimatedYear 2026
  (from wv-tax-tsd-365-2026
    (annual_rate 1150 :at interest-rates)))

; A tax year's rules: its figures, and what the IT-140ESI and the Code give
; it.
(defstruct WestVirginiaEstimatedRules
  (figures WestVirginiaEstimatedYear)
  ; IT-210 Part I line 5: no penalty when tax after credits less withholding
  ; is under it.
  (threshold Money)
  ; IT-210 Part I lines 6 and 7: 90% of this year's tax and 100% of last
  ; year's, in basis points.
  (this_year_rate Int)
  (last_year_rate Int)
  ; IT-210 Part I line 8: this year's tax above which a zero tax last year no
  ; longer gives a target of zero.
  (no_liability_limit Money)
  ; IT-210 Part IV Section B: the daily factor it prints for each calendar
  ; year, in millionths a day, each charge in whole dollars.
  (daily (Slice EstRate))
  ; The IT-140ESI's 10% of this year's tax below which no payments are
  ; required, in basis points.
  (small_share Int)
  ; The IT-140ESI's due dates, before moving.
  (due_dates (Slice Date))
  ; IT-210 Part IV line 1: a quarter of Part I line 8 by each date, and
  ; withholding spread in the same shares, in basis points.
  (shares (Slice Int))
  ; W. Va. Code § 2-2-1's holidays, which move a date.
  (holidays (Slice Date))
  ; § 11-21-55(d): a requirement first met after this day gets fewer
  ; instalments, which IT-210 does not apply.
  (late_start_after Date)
  ; § 11-10-18a(i): the last day of January, before moving.
  (file_and_pay_by Date)
  ; The penalty runs no later than April 15 of the next year.
  (stop Date)
  ; IT-210 Part II: the period ends and line 11's applicable percentages.
  (period_ends (Slice Date))
  (annualised_shares (Slice Int))
  (explanation ret/EstimatedExplanation))

; How West Virginia's estimated tax works, written by hand for the years
; these rules carry.
(= wv-estimated-explanation ret/EstimatedExplanation
  (est-explanation
    "West Virginia expects estimated payments if withholding leaves $600 or more due. The penalty is interest on each quarter's shortfall, at 11.5% a year for 2026."
    ["You avoid the penalty if withholding and estimated payments reach a target. The target is the smaller of 90% of this year's tax or 100% of last year's. A quarter of it is due by each date. Last year's figure counts only if that return covered a full 12 months. There is no 110% tier for higher incomes. A zero tax last year counts only while this year's tax is $5,000 or less. Then the penalty form asks for nothing. Above that, you need 90% of this year's tax."
     "The due dates are April 15, June 15, September 15 and the next January 15. A date on a weekend or a legal holiday becomes the next business day. Withholding counts as paid evenly across the four dates. You can instead show when it was actually withheld. Filing and paying in full by the end of January excuses the January payment. For 2026 that means by Monday, February 1, 2027."
     "The penalty is charged daily on each date's shortfall. It runs until the shortfall is paid or April 15 of the next year. A payment goes first to the oldest shortfall. The rate is set once a year at the prime rate plus three points. The form prints it as a daily factor, 0.000315 for 2026. Form IT-210's annualized method can lower early quarters for uneven income. The Tax Division can waive the penalty for a casualty or for reasonable cause."]
    "West Virginia differs from federal in ways that change a number. Its threshold is $600, not the federal $1,000. It has no 110% prior-year tier. A zero tax last year counts only while this year's tax is $5,000 or less. The rate is set once a year, 11.5% for 2026, not each quarter. There's no waiver for retirement or disability."
    ["W. Va. Code §§ 11-21-55, 11-21-56, 11-10-17a, 11-10-18a and 2-2-1"
     "West Virginia Tax Division, IT-140ESI, Estimated Tax Payments Instructions (Sept 2023)"
     "West Virginia Tax Division, 2025 Personal Income Tax Forms and Instructions, including Form IT-210"
     "West Virginia Tax Division, TSD-365, How Interest and Additions to Tax are Assessed"]))

; The 2026 rules. No 2026 IT-140ES, IT-140ESI or IT-210 is published: the 10%
; test and the due dates are the IT-140ESI (Sept 2023)'s; the $600 threshold,
; the 90% and 100% tests, the $5,000 limit, the quarters, the annualised
; periods and percentages, the April 15 stop and the 0.000315 daily factor
; for 2026 the 2025 IT-210's,
; and the late-start day and the last day of January the Code's. The holidays
; are § 2-2-1(a)'s from the first due date to February 1, 2027, each moved
; under § 2-2-1(b), less election days and days the Governor proclaims,
; which no checked-in document dates; none falls on a date these rules move.
; A figure's source must be for its year, so these are written out rather
; than deffigures.
(= wv-estimated-rules-2026 WestVirginiaEstimatedRules
  (make-struct WestVirginiaEstimatedRules
    :figures wv-estimated-2026
    :threshold #usd"600.00"
    :this_year_rate 9000
    :last_year_rate 10000
    :no_liability_limit #usd"5000.00"
    :daily [(EstRate #date"2026-01-01" #date"2026-12-31" 315
                     "IT-210 (2025), Part IV Section B: 11.5%, 0.000315 a day, January 1 to December 31, 2026; TSD-365")]
    :small_share 1000
    :due_dates [#date"2026-04-15" #date"2026-06-15" #date"2026-09-15" #date"2027-01-15"]
    :shares [2500 2500 2500 2500]
    :holidays [#date"2026-05-25"   ; Memorial Day
               #date"2026-06-19"   ; West Virginia Day, June 20 falling on a Saturday
               #date"2026-07-03"   ; Independence Day, July 4 falling on a Saturday
               #date"2026-09-07"   ; Labor Day
               #date"2026-10-12"   ; Columbus Day
               #date"2026-11-11"   ; Veterans' Day
               #date"2026-11-26"   ; Thanksgiving Day
               #date"2026-11-27"   ; Lincoln's Day
               #date"2026-12-25"   ; Christmas Day
               #date"2027-01-01"   ; New Year's Day
               #date"2027-01-18"]  ; Martin Luther King's Birthday
    :late_start_after #date"2026-04-01"
    :file_and_pay_by #date"2027-01-31"
    :stop #date"2027-04-15"
    :period_ends [#date"2026-03-31" #date"2026-05-31" #date"2026-08-31" #date"2026-12-31"]
    :annualised_shares [2250 4500 6750 9000]
    :explanation wv-estimated-explanation))

(= wv-estimated-years (Table Int WestVirginiaEstimatedRules)
  (table 2026 wv-estimated-rules-2026))

; The form the worksheet holds.
(= wv-estimated-form String "Form IT-210, Underpayment of Estimated Tax by Individuals")

; "Aug 31" in the tax year and "Jan 15, 2027" outside it, as the Go rules
; write a date.
(def wv-short-date ((d Date) (year Int)) String
  :cite ()
  (if (is (date-year d) year)
      (concat [(elt est-short-month-names (- (date-month d) 1)) " " (int-to-string (date-day d))])
      (est-short-date d)))

(def wv-divergence ((rule String) (form String) (form-source String) (statute String)
                    (statute-source String) (uses ret/DivergenceReading) (affects Bool))
  ret/EstimatedDivergence
  :cite ()
  (proto 'ret/EstimatedDivergence
    :rule rule :form form :form_source form-source :statute statute :statute_source statute-source
    :uses uses :affects_household affects))

; Which divergences change these facts' figures or answers.
(defstruct WestVirginiaAffected
  (who_must_pay Bool)
  (prior_year Bool)
  (no_liability Bool)
  (late_start Bool)
  (january Bool)
  (daily_factor Bool)
  (withholding Bool))

; Where the Tax Division's documents and the Code part ways on a rule every
; West Virginia computation uses, each affecting the household only when its
; facts reach the rule.
(def wv-estimated-divergences ((r WestVirginiaEstimatedRules) (year Int) (in WestVirginiaAffected))
  (Slice ret/EstimatedDivergence)
  :cite ((law "W. Va. Code" "11-10-18a") (law "W. Va. Code" "11-21-55") (law "W. Va. Code" "11-10-17a"))
  [(wv-divergence "Who must make estimated payments"
     "Payments are required when tax less West Virginia withholding is $600 or more. The exception is a balance under 10% of this year's tax."
     "IT-140ESI (Sept 2023), Who must make estimated tax payments?; 2025 IT-140 booklet, Credit for Estimated Tax"
     "The test is your West Virginia income other than withheld wages. Payments are required if it's expected to exceed $400 plus personal exemptions. The law has no 10% test, and $600 is only the penalty exception."
     "W. Va. Code § 11-21-55(a); § 11-10-18a(e)(1)"
     'ret/DIVERGENCE_READING_FORM (. in 'who_must_pay))
   (wv-divergence "The prior-year test"
     "The target is the smaller of 90% of this year's tax and 100% of last year's. Each payment is a quarter of it. A quarter that misses the prior-year amount is charged only on what it missed."
     "IT-210 (2025), Part I lines 6 to 8 and Part IV line 1"
     "The shortfall is measured against a quarter of 90% of this year's tax. Last year's tax excuses a quarter only if payments to date reach its share."
     "W. Va. Code § 11-10-18a(b)(1) and (d)(1)"
     'ret/DIVERGENCE_READING_FORM (. in 'prior_year))
   (wv-divergence "No liability last year"
     "A zero tax last year means no payments while this year's tax is $5,000 or less. There's no condition of US citizenship or residence."
     "IT-210 (2025), Part I line 8"
     "The penalty is excused only if last year's West Virginia tax was zero. Last year must be 12 months, spent as a US citizen or resident. This year's tax must be under $5,000. Otherwise 90% of this year's tax applies. The booklet says the same."
     "W. Va. Code § 11-10-18a(d)(1) and (e)(2); 2025 IT-140 booklet, Exceptions to the Penalty"
     'ret/DIVERGENCE_READING_FORM (. in 'no_liability))
   (wv-divergence "A requirement first met after April 1"
     "A quarter of the year's amount is due by every date for every filer."
     "IT-210 (2025), Part II line 15 and Part IV line 1"
     "First meeting the requirement after April 1 gives fewer, equal installments. That's three from June 15, two from September 15, or all on January 15. The penalty divides 90% of the tax by that number."
     "W. Va. Code §§ 11-21-55(d), 11-21-56(a); § 11-10-18a(b)(1)"
     'ret/DIVERGENCE_READING_FORM (. in 'late_start))
   (wv-divergence "A return filed and paid by January 31"
     "The booklet excuses the January payment if you file and pay by February 1. The IT-140ESI says by January 31."
     "2025 IT-140 booklet, Exceptions to the Penalty; IT-210 (2025), Part IV line 2 instructions; IT-140ESI (Sept 2023), For Your Information"
     "Filing and paying in full by the end of January excuses the January payment. A weekend or holiday moves that date to the next business day. Jan 31, 2027 is a Sunday, so the date is Monday, Feb 1, 2027."
     "W. Va. Code § 11-10-18a(i); § 2-2-1(e)"
     'ret/DIVERGENCE_READING_STATUTE (. in 'january))
   (wv-divergence "The daily interest factor"
     "Each day is charged at a printed factor of 0.000315. That's 11.5% divided by 365, rounded to six places."
     "IT-210 (2025), Part IV Section B and line 11 instructions"
     (concat ["The charge is the yearly rate on the shortfall for its period, "
              (est-percent (. r 'figures.annual_rate)) " for " (int-to-string year) ". That's 0.00031507 a day."])
     "W. Va. Code §§ 11-10-17a(c), 11-10-18a(a); TSD-365"
     'ret/DIVERGENCE_READING_FORM (. in 'daily_factor))
   ; The IT-140ESI's 8% floor is below the 2026 rate, and no six-month rate
   ; is published, so both readings give the same rate.
   (wv-divergence "How the rate is set"
     "The IT-140ESI says the rate is set every six months and can't be less than 8%."
     "IT-140ESI (Sept 2023), What if I don't pay enough estimated tax?"
     "Since 2017 the rate is set once a year, from January 1. It's the adjusted prime rate plus three points. The 8% floor applies only to years before 2017."
     "W. Va. Code § 11-10-17a(a) and (c)"
     'ret/DIVERGENCE_READING_STATUTE false)
   (wv-divergence "Withholding on the dates withheld"
     "One box in Part I puts all withholding on the dates it was withheld. Otherwise a quarter of it counts on each date."
     "IT-210 (2025), Part I and Part IV line 2 instructions"
     "Wage withholding and other withholding may each be put on their actual dates. Either may instead be spread evenly, separately from the other."
     "W. Va. Code § 11-10-18a(g)"
     'ret/DIVERGENCE_READING_FORM (. in 'withholding))])

; The requirement, the due dates, what IT-210 Part IV line 1 requires on each
; (nothing in January for a return filed and paid by the moved January 31),
; the credits, and the questions and divergences the requirement reports.
(defstruct WestVirginiaAssessment
  (req EstRequirement)
  (exempt Bool)
  (dues (Slice Date))
  (required (Slice Money))
  (ai (Slice fed/Form2210.AnnualizationPeriod))
  (credits (Slice EstCredit))
  (excused_january Bool)
  (questions (Slice ret/EstimatedQuestion))
  (divergences (Slice ret/EstimatedDivergence)))

; Whether estimated payments are needed and the required annual payment
; (§ 11-10-18a(b), (d) and (e); IT-210 Part I; the IT-140ESI), the due dates
; and what each requires (§ 11-21-56(a); IT-210 Parts II and IV), and the
; January instalment a return filed early excuses (§ 11-10-18a(i)).
(def wv-estimated-assess ((inputs ret/ReturnInputs) (f EstFacts) (r WestVirginiaEstimatedRules)) WestVirginiaAssessment
  :cite ((law "W. Va. Code" "11-10-18a" "(b)") (law "W. Va. Code" "11-10-18a" "(d)")
         (law "W. Va. Code" "11-10-18a" "(e)") (law "W. Va. Code" "11-10-18a" "(i)")
         (law "W. Va. Code" "11-21-56" "(a)")
         (doc "wv-tax-tsd-365-2026" "interest-rates"))
  (withs (y r
          est (. inputs 'estimated_tax)
          year (. f 'tax_year)
          year-s (int-to-string year)
          last-s (int-to-string (- year 1))
          none ((inst empty-slice ret/EstimatedQuestion))
          holidays (. r 'holidays)
          dues (est-move-dates (. r 'due_dates) holidays)
          known (. f 'tax_known)
          tax (. f 'tax)
          withheld (. f 'withheld)
          threshold (. y 'threshold)
          limit (. y 'no_liability_limit)
          this-rate (. y 'this_year_rate)
          last-rate (. y 'last_year_rate)
          p (. f 'prior)
          has-prior (. p 'on_record)
          status (. p 'status)
          prior-tax (. p 'tax)
          ; § 11-10-18a(e)(2)(C): a United States citizen or resident all of
          ; last year, EstimatedTaxInputs.prior_year_us_citizen_or_resident.
          us-answered (has? est 'prior_year_us_citizen_or_resident)
          us (. est 'prior_year_us_citizen_or_resident)
          ; IT-210 Part I line 6: 90% of this year's tax after credits.
          this-amount (est-rate-of this-rate tax)
          this-option (if known
                          (est-this-year-option this-rate this-amount "IT-210 (2025), Part I line 6")
                          (est-unavailable (est-this-year-option this-rate #usd"0.00" "IT-210 (2025), Part I line 6")
                                           est-needs-this-year-tax))
          ; IT-210 Part I lines 7 and 8: last year's tax after credits, for a
          ; 12-month return, and the rule for a zero.
          closed (fn ((why String)) ret/EstimatedTargetOption
                   (est-unavailable (est-last-year-option last-rate #usd"0.00" "IT-210 (2025), Part I line 7") why))
          short-year (and has-prior (is status 'ret/EstimatedTaxInputs.PRIOR_RETURN_SHORT_YEAR))
          not-required (and has-prior (is status 'ret/EstimatedTaxInputs.PRIOR_RETURN_NOT_REQUIRED))
          not-filed (and has-prior (is status 'ret/EstimatedTaxInputs.PRIOR_RETURN_NOT_FILED))
          full-year (and has-prior (is status 'ret/EstimatedTaxInputs.PRIOR_RETURN_FULL_YEAR))
          zero (and full-year (is prior-tax #usd"0.00"))
          prior-option (if (not has-prior)
                           (closed (concat ["Needs your " last-s " West Virginia return"]))
                           short-year
                           (closed (concat ["Your " last-s " West Virginia return covered less than 12 months, not a full 12"]))
                           (or not-required not-filed)
                           (closed (concat ["You didn't file a " last-s " West Virginia return"]))
                           (and zero (not known))
                           (closed (concat ["A zero " last-s " West Virginia tax counts only if this year's tax is "
                                            (est-whole limit) " or less"]))
                           (and zero (> tax limit))
                           (closed (concat ["A zero " last-s " West Virginia tax doesn't count if this year's tax is over "
                                            (est-whole limit)]))
                           zero
                           (est-last-year-option last-rate #usd"0.00" "IT-210 (2025), Part I lines 7 and 8")
                           (est-last-year-option last-rate (est-rate-of last-rate prior-tax) "IT-210 (2025), Part I line 7"))
          ; No return was required: the booklet's Exceptions to the Penalty,
          ; which agrees with § 11-10-18a(e)(2).
          no-liability (or (and not-required known (< tax limit) us-answered us)
                           (and zero known (<= tax limit)))
          line-eight-only (and zero known (<= tax limit) (not (and us-answered us (< tax limit))))
          tax-needed-for (if (and not-required (not known))
                             (concat ["With no West Virginia tax for " last-s ", you're excused if it's under " (est-whole limit) "."])
                             (and zero (not known))
                             (concat ["Your zero " last-s " tax counts only if it's " (est-whole limit) " or less."])
                             "")
          prior-open (is (. prior-option 'status) 'ret/OPTION_STATUS_AVAILABLE)
          prior-amount (. prior-option 'amount)
          use-prior (and prior-open (or (not known) (< prior-amount this-amount)))
          chosen-id (if use-prior (. prior-option 'id) (. this-option 'id))
          target (if use-prior prior-amount this-amount)
          options [this-option prior-option]
          ; Asked only when no exception sets the target.
          asks (append
                 (if (not has-prior)
                     [(est-ask "prior year return"
                               (concat ["What was the tax after credits on your " last-s " West Virginia return?"])
                               "With it, 100% of last year's tax could be your target.")]
                     (and not-required known (< tax limit) (not us-answered))
                     [(est-ask "jurisdiction fact"
                               (concat ["Were you a US citizen or resident all of " last-s "?"])
                               (concat ["If so, a zero tax that year and under " (est-whole limit)
                                        " this year excuses the penalty."]))]
                     none)
                 (if known
                     none
                     [(est-ask "this year's tax"
                               (concat ["What do you expect your " year-s " West Virginia tax after credits to be?"])
                               (concat ["With it, 90% of this year's tax could be your target and the " (est-whole threshold)
                                        " test used." (if (is tax-needed-for "") "" (concat [" " tax-needed-for]))]))]))
          owed (- tax withheld)
          small (est-rate-of (. r 'small_share) tax)
          req (if (and known (< owed threshold))
                  (est-exempt options
                    (est-exception-below "exception-under-threshold" "Tax less withholding" threshold
                                         "W. Va. Code § 11-10-18a(e)(1); IT-210 (2025), Part I line 5")
                    (if (< owed #usd"0.00")
                        (concat ["Withholding of " (est-whole withheld) " covers your West Virginia tax of " (est-whole tax)
                                 ". That " (est-leaves owed) ", so no estimated payments are needed."])
                        (is owed #usd"0.00")
                        (concat ["Your withholding of " (est-whole withheld) " covers your West Virginia tax of "
                                 (est-whole tax) ". No estimated payments are needed."])
                        (is (est-whole owed) (est-whole threshold))
                        (concat ["Your West Virginia tax less withholding is just under " (est-whole threshold)
                                 ". No estimated payments are needed."])
                        (concat ["Your West Virginia tax of " (est-whole tax) " less " (est-whole withheld) " withheld leaves "
                                 (est-whole owed) ". That's under " (est-whole threshold) ", so no estimated payments are needed."])))
                  no-liability
                  (est-exempt options
                    (est-exception "exception-no-west-virginia-tax-due-last-year" "No West Virginia tax due last year"
                                   "W. Va. Code § 11-10-18a(e)(2); IT-210 (2025), Part I lines 7 and 8")
                    (concat ["You had no West Virginia tax for " last-s ", and your " year-s " tax is " (est-whole tax)
                             ". No estimated payments are needed, and no penalty can arise."]))
                  (and (not known) (not prior-open))
                  (est-no-target options
                    (concat ["Your " last-s " return doesn't give a target. Your target is 90% of your " year-s
                             " West Virginia tax, unless an exception applies."]))
                  (and (not known) (>= withheld target))
                  (est-choose options chosen-id false
                    (concat ["Your withholding of " (est-whole withheld) " reaches " (est-percent last-rate) " of your "
                             last-s " tax, " (est-whole target) ". No estimated payments are needed, whatever your "
                             year-s " tax is."]))
                  (not known)
                  (est-choose options chosen-id true
                    (concat ["Your target is " (est-percent last-rate) " of your " last-s " West Virginia tax, "
                             (est-whole target) ". That keeps you clear of a penalty whatever your " year-s
                             " tax turns out to be. "
                             (if (> withheld #usd"0.00")
                                 (concat ["After " (est-whole withheld) " of withholding, that's " (est-whole (- target withheld))
                                          " of estimated payments. Pay a quarter by each date."])
                                 "Pay it in estimated payments, a quarter by each date.")]))
                  (and (>= withheld target) (< owed small))
                  (est-choose options chosen-id false
                    (if (is (est-whole owed) (est-whole small))
                        (concat ["Your West Virginia withholding leaves just less than " (est-percent (. r 'small_share))
                                 " of your " (est-whole tax) " tax. No estimated payments are needed. Withholding already reaches the "
                                 (est-whole target) " required."])
                        (concat ["Your West Virginia withholding of " (est-whole withheld) " leaves " (est-whole owed)
                                 " of tax. That's less than " (est-percent (. r 'small_share)) " of your " (est-whole tax)
                                 " tax, so no estimated payments are needed. Withholding already reaches the "
                                 (est-whole target) " required."])))
                  (>= withheld target)
                  (est-choose options chosen-id false
                    (concat ["Your West Virginia withholding of " (est-whole withheld) " covers the year's "
                             (est-whole target) " target. No estimated payments are needed."]))
                  (is withheld #usd"0.00")
                  (est-choose options chosen-id true
                    (concat ["Your West Virginia tax of " (est-whole tax) " is " (est-whole threshold)
                             " or more, with no withholding. You need estimated payments of " (est-whole target)
                             ", a quarter by each date."]))
                  (est-choose options chosen-id true
                    (concat ["Your West Virginia tax of " (est-whole tax) " less " (est-whole withheld) " withheld leaves "
                             (est-whole owed) ". That's " (est-whole threshold) " or more, and withholding is short of the "
                             (est-whole target) " required. You need estimated payments of " (est-whole (- target withheld))
                             ", a quarter by each date."])))
          exempt (is (. req 'status) 'ret/REQUIREMENT_STATUS_EXEMPT)
          scheduled (and (not exempt) (est-target-known req))
          regular (est-increments (est-cumulative target (. r 'shares)))
          periods (. f 'periods)
          ai (if (or (not scheduled) (empty? periods))
                 ((inst empty-slice fed/Form2210.AnnualizationPeriod))
                 (est-schedule-ai
                   (map (fn ((pt ret/EstimatedTaxInputs.CallerEstimate.PeriodTax)) Money (. pt 'annualised_tax))
                        periods)
                   (. r 'annualised_shares)
                   regular))
          instalments (if (not scheduled)
                          (map (fn ((d Date)) Money #usd"0.00") dues)
                          (empty? ai)
                          regular
                          (map (fn ((ap fed/Form2210.AnnualizationPeriod)) Money (. ap 'required_installment)) ai))
          ; January 31, 2027 is a Sunday. § 2-2-1(e) moves it to February 1,
          ; the date the 2025 booklet prints.
          pay-by (next-business-day (. r 'file_and_pay_by) holidays)
          filed-set (. f 'return_filed_set)
          filed (. f 'return_filed)
          excused (and scheduled filed-set (<= filed pay-by))
          last (- (len instalments) 1)
          required (map (fn ((i Int)) Money (if (and excused (is i last)) #usd"0.00" (elt instalments i)))
                        (est-range (len instalments)))
          credits (est-credits f dues (. r 'shares))
          ledger (est-apply dues required credits)
          short (and scheduled (some (fn ((e EstLedgerEntry)) Bool (> (. e 'shortfall) #usd"0.00")) ledger))
          met (. est 'requirement_first_met)
          in (make-struct WestVirginiaAffected
               :who_must_pay (is (. req 'status) 'ret/REQUIREMENT_STATUS_REQUIRED)
               :prior_year (and (not exempt) (est-target-known req) use-prior short)
               :no_liability line-eight-only
               :late_start (and scheduled (has? est 'requirement_first_met) (> met (. r 'late_start_after)))
               :january (and scheduled filed-set (is filed pay-by) (!= pay-by (. r 'file_and_pay_by)))
               :daily_factor short
               :withholding (and scheduled (> withheld #usd"0.00"))))
    (make-struct WestVirginiaAssessment
      :req req
      :exempt exempt
      :dues dues
      :required required
      :ai ai
      :credits credits
      :excused_january excused
      :questions (if exempt none asks)
      :divergences (wv-estimated-divergences r year in))))

; Each instalment's running totals as the ledger has them, with the January
; one excused when a return filed early excused it.
(def wv-estimated-schedule ((a WestVirginiaAssessment)) (Slice ret/EstimatedInstallment)
  :cite ()
  (withs (ledger (est-apply (. a 'dues) (. a 'required) (. a 'credits))
          last (- (len ledger) 1))
    (map (fn ((i Int)) ret/EstimatedInstallment
           (withs (e (elt ledger i))
             (est-installment (+ i 1) (. e 'due) (. e 'needed_by) (. e 'credited_by) (. e 'shortfall)
                              (and (. a 'excused_january) (is i last)))))
         (est-range (len ledger)))))

; The penalty lines as IT-210 Part IV Section B figures them: each piece of
; each shortfall at the printed daily factor for its days, from the due date
; to the day it was paid or to stop, whichever is earlier, each charge in
; whole dollars. Days no factor covers aren't charged; the result says the
; first.
(def wv-factor-penalty ((ledger (Slice EstLedgerEntry)) (stop Date) (factors (Slice EstRate))) EstLines
  :cite ((law "W. Va. Code" "11-10-18a" "(a)") (law "W. Va. Code" "11-10-18a" "(c)"))
  (fold (fn ((acc EstLines) (e EstLedgerEntry)) EstLines
          (if (<= (. e 'shortfall) #usd"0.00")
              acc
              (withs (due (. e 'due)
                      lining (fold (fn ((l EstLining) (pc EstPiece)) EstLining
                                     (withs (to (if (. pc 'paid) (min (. pc 'paid_on) stop) stop))
                                       (if (<= to due)
                                           l
                                           (withs (a (est-daily-factor (. pc 'amount) due to factors true)
                                                   u (est-first-unrated (. l 'rated) (. l 'unrated) (. a 'rated) (. a 'unrated)))
                                             (EstLining (append (. l 'parts) (. a 'parts))
                                                        (max (. l 'last) to)
                                                        (. u 'rated)
                                                        (. u 'unrated))))))
                                   (EstLining ((inst empty-slice EstPart)) due true due)
                                   (. e 'pieces))
                      u (est-first-unrated (. acc 'rated) (. acc 'unrated) (. lining 'rated) (. lining 'unrated)))
                (EstLines (append (. acc 'lines)
                                  [(EstLine (. e 'number) due (. e 'shortfall)
                                            (days-between due (. lining 'last))
                                            (. lining 'parts)
                                            (est-line-total (. lining 'parts)))])
                          (. u 'rated)
                          (. u 'unrated)))))
        (EstLines ((inst empty-slice EstLine)) true stop)
        ledger))

; The penalty to as_of: each shortfall at the daily factor for its calendar
; year, by the day, from its due date until paid, the return was filed with
; the balance, or April 15 of the next year, whichever is earliest. The Tax
; Commissioner may waive it for a casualty (§ 11-10-18a(e)(3)); there is no
; waiver for retirement or disability, only for reasonable cause.
(def wv-estimated-penalty ((f EstFacts) (r WestVirginiaEstimatedRules) (a WestVirginiaAssessment)) EstPenaltyResult
  :cite ((law "W. Va. Code" "11-10-18a" "(a)") (law "W. Va. Code" "11-10-18a" "(e)")
         (doc "wv-tax-tsd-365-2026" "interest-rates"))
  (withs (none ((inst empty-slice ret/EstimatedQuestion))
          year (. f 'tax_year)
          latest (min (. f 'as_of) (. r 'stop))
          stop (if (and (. f 'return_filed_set) (< (. f 'return_filed) latest)) (. f 'return_filed) latest)
          w (. f 'waiver)
          cause (. w 'cause)
          claimed (and (. f 'waiver_answered)
                       (!= cause 'ret/EstimatedTaxInputs.WAIVER_CAUSE_NONE)
                       (!= cause 'ret/EstimatedTaxInputs.WAIVER_CAUSE_UNSPECIFIED))
          casualty (or (is cause 'ret/EstimatedTaxInputs.WAIVER_CAUSE_CASUALTY)
                       (is cause 'ret/EstimatedTaxInputs.WAIVER_CAUSE_DISASTER)))
    (if (. a 'exempt)
        (EstPenaltyResult (est-penalty stop (est-no-lines stop) false "" est-no-waiver) none)
        (withs (pl (wv-factor-penalty (est-apply (. a 'dues) (. a 'required) (. a 'credits))
                                      stop (. r 'daily))
                penalty (est-penalty stop pl (not (. f 'tax_known)) ""
                                     (if (not claimed)
                                         est-no-waiver
                                         casualty
                                         (est-standard-waiver f "The Tax Commissioner" 62)
                                         (EstWaiver true 'ret/WAIVER_OUTCOME_UNDECIDED
                                                    "West Virginia has no waiver for retirement or disability. The Tax Division can waive the penalty if you show reasonable cause.")))
                charged (> (. penalty 'total) #usd"0.00"))
          (EstPenaltyResult
            penalty
            (append
              (if (. pl 'rated)
                  none
                  [(est-ask "unpublished rate" ""
                            (concat ["The rate for the days after " (wv-short-date (date-add-days (. pl 'unrated) -1) year)
                                     " isn't published yet."]))])
              (if (and charged claimed (not casualty))
                  [(est-ask "unsettled rule" ""
                            "West Virginia's rules don't say if retiring or disability is reasonable cause. Reasonable cause lets the Tax Division waive the penalty.")]
                  none)))))))

; Why these facts can't be answered under these rules, or "": the annualised
; method's periods must be IT-210 Part II's.
(def wv-estimated-refusal ((f EstFacts) (r WestVirginiaEstimatedRules)) String
  :cite ((law "W. Va. Code" "11-10-18a" "(d)(2)"))
  (withs (periods (. f 'periods)
          ends (. r 'period_ends))
    (if (> (len periods) (len ends))
        (concat ["westvirginiataxcalc: IT-210 Part II has " (int-to-string (len ends)) " periods, not " (int-to-string (len periods))])
        (fold (fn ((acc String) (i Int)) String
                (withs (given (. (elt periods i) 'end))
                  (if (or (!= acc "") (is given (elt ends i)))
                      acc
                      (concat ["westvirginiataxcalc: IT-210 Part II period " (int-to-string (+ i 1)) " ends on "
                               (est-iso-date (elt ends i)) ", not " (est-iso-date given)]))))
              ""
              (est-range (len periods))))))

; West Virginia's answer under one year's rules.
(def wv-estimated-answer-for ((inputs ret/ReturnInputs) (r WestVirginiaEstimatedRules)) ret/EstimatedAnswer
  :cite ((law "W. Va. Code" "11-10-18a"))
  (withs (f (est-facts inputs "WV" (est-state-prior inputs "WV"))
          refusal (wv-estimated-refusal f r))
    (if (!= refusal "")
        (est-not-answered "WV" 'ret/ESTIMATED_OUTCOME_REFUSED refusal)
        (withs (a (wv-estimated-assess inputs f r)
                explanation (. r 'explanation))
          (if (not (est-target-known (. a 'req)))
              (est-answer-unknown "WV" (. a 'req) (. f 'tax_known) (. a 'questions) (. a 'divergences) explanation)
              (withs (pen (wv-estimated-penalty f r a))
                (proto-with
                  (est-answer "WV" (. f 'as_of) (. a 'req) (. f 'tax_known)
                    (wv-estimated-schedule a)
                    (. pen 'penalty)
                    (if (est-nothing-planned f)
                        (. pen 'penalty)
                        (. (wv-estimated-penalty (est-facts-made f) r a) 'penalty))
                    (append (. a 'questions) (. pen 'questions))
                    (. a 'divergences)
                    explanation)
                  :pattern (est-pattern wv-estimated-form
                             (est-form-2210 f (. a 'req) (. a 'dues) (. a 'required) (. a 'credits)
                                            (. a 'ai) (. pen 'penalty))))))))))

; West Virginia's answer: no rules for a year with no figures, and a farmer,
; who makes one payment by January 15 at 66 2/3%, not yet covered.
(def west-virginia-estimated-answer ((inputs ret/ReturnInputs)) ret/EstimatedAnswer
  :cite ((law "W. Va. Code" "11-10-18a"))
  (withs (year (. inputs 'tax_year)
          r (lookup wv-estimated-years year)
          problem (est-input-problem inputs)
          ff (. inputs 'estimated_tax.farming_and_fishing)
          gross (. ff 'this_year_gross_income))
    (if (nil? r)
        (est-no-rules "WV" year)
        (!= problem "")
        (est-not-answered "WV" (est-input-outcome inputs) problem)
        (and (> gross #usd"0.00") (>= (* (. ff 'this_year_farming) 3) (* gross 2)))
        (est-not-answered "WV" 'ret/ESTIMATED_OUTCOME_UNSUPPORTED
          "estimated: these facts need rules this build does not implement: a farmer with two-thirds of gross income from farming makes one payment by January 15 at 66 2/3%, which is not built")
        (wv-estimated-answer-for inputs r))))
